### UX & Copywriting
**Risk:** `TERMINAL_REFUSALS` includes `'NOT_FOUND'`, but `reversalMemo` matches on `'RECEIPT_NOT_FOUND'`. When a terminal reversal occurs with reason `'NOT_FOUND'` and no custom `outcome.message` is supplied, `reversalMemo` falls through to generic fallback copy (`'Refunded — this cross-community purchase could not be completed'`) instead of explaining that the other community did not complete the sale. Similarly, `'BAD_SIGNATURE'` and `'RECEIPT_MISMATCH'` lack specific memo entries.

**Suggested Fix:**
Update `reversalMemo` to include `'NOT_FOUND'`, `'BAD_SIGNATURE'`, and `'RECEIPT_MISMATCH'`:
```typescript
function reversalMemo(reason: string): string {
    switch (reason) {
        case 'CAPACITY_LAPSED':
            return 'Refunded — the other community had reached its credit limit';
        case 'NOT_FOUND':
        case 'RECEIPT_NOT_FOUND':
            return 'Refunded — the other community did not complete the sale';
        case 'BAD_SIGNATURE':
        case 'RECEIPT_MISMATCH':
            return 'Refunded — invalid transaction verification from peer community';
        default:
            return 'Refunded — this cross-community purchase could not be completed';
    }
}
```
